{
  "name": "Gray-Scott Species: heredity",
  "description": "The Lineages heredity test with species instead: four walled circles, each seeded with one species (spots, worms, maze, curly), which never blend. Open doors with the Unwall tool (key 8). cross is 0 (the default): only same-species pairs reproduce. In the lab, doors opened at 30k: by 150k maze kept its own circle and maze and curly shared everything else (about 55/45) as interleaved territories, each keeping its own pattern; spots and worms died out. Set cross to 1 (as plain Gray-Scott) and curly, the species with the lowest death rate (F + k), takes every mixed cell and the whole field within 20k steps. Tint = local mean feed (P_F); view b1…b4 to see one species.",
